Which of the following lines is a tangent to the circle with equation
$$x^{2}+y^{2}=4\,?$$

(a) $x+y=2$;
(b) $y=x-2\sqrt{2}$;
(c) $x=\sqrt{2}$;
(d) $y=\sqrt{2}-x$.

Let $N=2^{k}\times 4^{m}\times 8^{n}$ where $k,m,n$ are positive whole numbers. Then $N$ will definitely be a square number whenever

(a) $k$ is even;
(b) $k+n$ is odd;
(c) $k$ is odd but $m+n$ is even;
(d) $k+n$ is even.

Which one of the following equations could possibly have the graph given below?

(a) $y=(3-x)^{2}(3+x)^{2}(1-x)$;
(b) $y=-x^{2}(x-9)\left(x^{2}-3\right)$;
(c) $y=(x-6)(x-2)^{2}(x+2)^{2}$;
(d) $y=\left(x^{2}-1\right)^{2}(3-x)$.

